        "reviewed_sha": "c0488b478cdbd79629bd6bcb88b5174c2f2375a7",
        "notes": "Author dispensation. The `Real.sqrt 5` at line 70 is the **cyclotomic normalisation** of the 5th-root-of-unity Lagrange resolvent (`(1/√5) * Σ ζ^(k·j) * x_j` is the standard discrete Fourier kernel over ℤ/5). The √5 is an algebraic-integer norm of ℚ(ζ_5)/ℚ — categorical content of the cyclotomic-field decomposition — NOT an archimedean evaluation at the substrate q_0. The q-usage detector regex catches `Real.sqrt` without knowing the radicand is a small concrete integer. Block remains categorical; the resolvent is a fixed Hecke-algebra construction independent of the substrate parameter."
      }
